    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T11:21:53Z",
    "body": "The two app tests from post-merge run 45013742033 (merge 92935735e of PR #3108). Panic text on origin/main 62353ac75, debug:\n\n```\nblind_slot_pocket_family_cuts_from_end_wall_to_stock_edge\npanicked at crates\\app\\tests\\blind_slot.rs:142:13:\nassertion `left == right` failed: Adaptive2D\n  left: 1\n right: 0\n```\n\n```\nadaptive2d_spiral_and_offset2d_support_relief_while_trochoidal_and_do_not_touch_refuse\npanicked at crates\\app\\tests\\corner_relief_safety.rs:177:5:\nadaptive2d dogbone verify must be silent: [StrategyFallback { at: 2, areas: 1 }]\n```\n\nCause: PR #3108 makes an Adaptive fallback to the Offset rings an advisory `StrategyFallback` warning. These two tests still expect zero warnings. The only warning is `StrategyFallback`, and its `areas` agrees with the fallback notes (`machining2d::rings_fallbacks`). So the product is correct. I adapt the two assertions with the pattern of #3108: accept only `StrategyFallback` with the same area count as the notes, require that it does not block the post, and keep all other checks.\n",
